# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# What is NOT published. The root is DENY-BY-DEFAULT: `/*` hides every root
# entry and the block below re-admits exactly the 25 that publish.
#
# Why deny-by-default, and ONLY at the root: this repository is public from its
# first commit and its history can never be rewritten, so a conventional
# deny-list -- where inclusion is the default -- makes anything nobody thought
# to exclude permanent on the first `git add -A`. Root-only strictness keeps
# normal tracking inside the language roots, so a new wrapper still appears in
# `git status`.
#
# This list must equal .github/root-manifest.txt, and
# .github/scripts/check-root-visibility.sh asserts that they agree.
#
# PRECISELY WHAT THAT GATE PROVES, now that the root denies by default. It sees
# only what git will publish. A stray root file with no `!` line here is
# invisible to it -- and that is correct rather than a hole, because such a file
# is also not stageable by `git add -A`, so it cannot reach the public surface
# at all. The gate therefore catches the two things that CAN change that
# surface: an entry re-admitted here but absent from the manifest (APPEARED),
# and an entry in the manifest that stopped being re-admitted (VANISHED). Both
# were verified with a planted defect when this file was written.

/*

!/.coderabbit.yaml
!/.dockerignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.github
!/.gitignore
!/.gitleaks.toml
!/.pre-commit-config.yaml
!/.python-version
!/ARCHITECTURE.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CITATION.cff
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/Dockerfile
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/backend
!/deploy
!/docs
!/engine
!/frontend
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.lock

# ---- working files, never published -----------------------------------------
# Redundant against `/*` above and kept deliberately: an explicit deny states
# the intent, so re-admitting one of these has to be a conscious act.
CLAUDE.md
todo.md
.claude/
.private/

# ---- local tool caches ------------------------------------------------------
.fastembed_cache/
.token-optimizer/
.import_linter_cache/

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
# THE GENERATED TIER IS NOT LISTED HERE, AND THAT IS THE POINT.
# `engine/src/econflow_engine/generated/` is machine-written by
# `scripts/gen_schemas.py`, and the reflex with generated code is to ignore it.
# It is COMMITTED deliberately: the generated form is what gets reviewed in a
# diff, and the artifact-drift gate re-emits it in `--check` mode and compares
# byte for byte. Ignoring it would delete the review surface and leave the gate
# comparing the generator against itself.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
build/
*.egg-info/

# ---- TypeScript (frontend/) -------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- OS / editor ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*~
